# --- Go ---
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# --- Build & deps (fetched by scripts/fetch-deps.ps1, see docs/specs/SPEC-11) ---
third_party/
deps/
build/

# --- Frontend (built artifacts only; frontend/ source is tracked) ---
node_modules/
# dist/ is a build product, but go:embed needs the directory to exist in a clean
# checkout (ticket 77 AC#1), so one anchor file stays tracked; panel.Assets.
# Built() reports false while the bundle is only that anchor, and the host shows
# an "assets not built" state instead of ever rendering it.
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep
assets/web/dist/

# --- Runtime data (never commit local data dirs) ---
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
data/
data-dev/
portable.txt

# --- Secrets (C28: API keys must never be plaintext in repo) ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/

# --- Test outputs ---
*.prof
coverage*
testdata/local/

# --- Git worktrees ---
# A worktree is a full second checkout of this repo. It must never show up as
# untracked noise in the main checkout's `git status`, and it must never be
# scanned: the D22 and panel hygiene instruments walk fixed paths from the repo
# root, and a nested copy of the tree under it would double their scope.
# `/` anchors to the root so a nested `.worktrees` inside a subproject is not
# swallowed by this rule.
.worktrees/

# --- IDE / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Repository-root junk (added 2026-10-26; reform plan 0-4, leg ignore-r1) ---
# Everything below is residue that was found sitting at the repository ROOT,
# not a convention: compiler output from ad-hoc C probes, output dumps from
# shell redirects that were typed into the wrong place, and directories that
# exist because a command redirected into something shaped like a flag.
# Every pattern is rooted ("/...") on purpose, so a legitimately named file or
# directory deeper in the tree is never swallowed by a root-only accident.
# Nothing was deleted to write this section (rule 8): the files still on disk
# are listed in docs/evidence/s1/ignore-r1-impl.md and wait for a one-shot
# sweep that the owner authorises.
#
# A PowerShell-style redirect that landed on disk instead of the null device.
/$null
#
# Flag-shaped names left behind by an argument that was never quoted.
/-
/-dummy
#
# gcc -S / gcc -c / windres residue from the C probes: 18 files whose mktemp
# prefixes came out as cc*/bcc*/Ccc*. The leading "/" is what makes a bare
# "*.s" safe here: Go assembly IS tracked (four files under
# .scratch/wisp/probes/220/*/), so an unanchored "*.s" would tell the next
# reader that tracked source is disposable. Root-only, and no tracked file
# lives at the root with these extensions.
/*.o
/*.s
/*.res
#
# Empty directories created by redirecting into a flag-like path. The last one
# really does carry a fullwidth colon (U+FF1A), not an ASCII one.
/cp/
/git/
/show/
/HEAD：cmd/
#
# Single output dumps: a portable-tests.sh run log, a `wc -l` tally, a grep
# hit, sparse punctuation, and a bare date from an unquoted argument.
/2379
/397
/4
/;
/2026-09-24
#
# Interleaved grep dumps from the ticket-154 trigger-gate probes. The middle
# word is not stable (state1/state2/nog6/stale), so it is matched by position:
# eight files, part<N>-<anything>-{fixed,pristine}.txt.
/part[0-9]*-*.txt
/core-after.*.txt
/g-f-*.txt
